A||||11||383GT||Swap Isuzu to Getrag in 87GT(new to forum)||||5||
Z||000000||383GT||12-13-2001||11:49 AM||||I am new to the Forum here, but have heard that a great deal of knowledge can be queried upon here.<BR>It appears that a 5sp Getrag can be put in instead of the current Isuzu 5 sp into an 87 GT.  Am I correct in saying that only the shift linkage needs to be changed in order for this to work?  Everything else can stay the same?  <BR>I am not sure why my 87 GT has the Isuzu 5sp.  I was under the impression that they came only with the Getrag…hmmm must have been swapped out.  Why that dirty b*$!)@# who sold it to me.  <P>Thanks in advance for the help.  I tried the search option, but didn’t find what I was looking for.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||lowfierogt||12-13-2001||11:59 AM||||For the cost of switching trannys.  Don't do it.   I have a 87 coupe V6 with the isuzu.  I like the tranny.  1 its cheap, two Tina has the isuzu in her v8 and does fine with 400 HP.   three you have to change slave cly.   four getrag is a lower gearing, means more gas money.   If it ant broke don't fix it.<P>hope this helps.<P>Welcome the the famliy.<P>Hope to see you around in Minnesota<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com/lowfierogtsig.gif">         <BR>http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com<BR>86 1/2 GT<BR>85 GT Project, fastback V8<BR>87 coupe Getting V6 daily driver over 300k miles||||reg||1
Z||000002||383GT||12-13-2001||01:34 PM||||Lowfierogt,<BR>Thanx for the input.  But it is broken,(I blew out 2nd gear) and I have an extra getrag tranny with ~42,000miles.  <BR>  So I also need the slave cylinder besides the shift linkage.  Is that all I would need to grab off my other one?  Do you think given that I have the Getrag tranny and it is broken that it is still not worth putting the Getrag in?  I just don't know how much an Isuzu will run. Thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||12-13-2001||01:52 PM||||383GT,<P>First question ... do you have a V8 in the car?<P>If so, the Isuzu has better gearing for the V8 and that is why it was used.  <P>Isuzu transaxles are very easy to find as opposed to the Getrag what you found.  <P>I found a place that I could have gotten 4 Isuzus for ~$200 but a Getrag is $400 and higher.<P>My thinking is, since you already have the Getrag, the slave, hopefully the shift cables (the shifter is the same), and the Getrag brackets, you might as well put it in.<P>If you do have the V8, buy an other Isuzu (or two  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) and put it back in and sell the Getrag ... there are many here who would take it off you hands (even me!).<P>LMK if you decide on the Isuzu and I will check if those transaxles are still available (and give you the info on who and where they are.)<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000004||383GT||12-13-2001||02:19 PM||||Yes, I am running a V8 in there. Thanks for the insight.  I will look for an Isuzu to put in there.  Do you know of any contacts that would still have any?  In that case I would want to get rid of that Getrag.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hartz||12-13-2001||02:59 PM||||First - Welcome aboard.  This forum is, indeed, a great source of info.<P>Secondly - COOL!  Another V8!  Woo hoo!  Let's see some pictures!  Let's hear some details!  Did I remember to ask for pictures?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Lastly, you CAN run a Getrag with a V8.  I won't go into the religious wars that can erupt over gearing issues and V8s (shudder) but the Getrag makes a decent choice IMO.  I have a 3.61 final drive ratio in mine, and she's just great.  Heck, some folks even go with the 4.10 four speeds!  It all depends on how you use the car and what you like.  If it's cheaper/easier for you to go with the tranny you have, I say go for it.<P>Best of luck,<P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com||||reg||14
Z||000006||jelly2m8||12-13-2001||03:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hartz:<BR><B><BR>Lastly, you CAN run a Getrag with a V8.  I won't go into the religious wars that can erupt over gearing issues and V8s (shudder) but the Getrag makes a decent choice IMO.  I have a 3.61 final drive ratio in mine, and she's just great.  Heck, some folks even go with the 4.10 four speeds!  It all depends on how you use the car and what you like.  If it's cheaper/easier for you to go with the tranny you have, I say go for it.<P>Best of luck,<P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well said Hartz, I'm behind ya 100% on this.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
